A||N||4||varnster||HELP, pioneer headunit muting wont stop!||||8||
Z||000000||varnster||01-06-2001||04:25 PM||||Im just finished installing amp,changer,speakers,and a pioneer deh-p47dh<BR>problem is as soon as I turn on the power,<BR>the headunit is saying mute I cant find a way<BR>to turn it off. Its for cell phone use, with a incoming call the unit self mutes but I dont have the wire hooked up for this feature, I think it operates by grounding the headunit so how do I trouble shoot this?||||reg||8
Z||000001||Oreif||01-06-2001||04:37 PM||||If the radio goes into "mute" mode then either the cell phone wire is being pinched and grounded or if you bought the radio used, someone used a remote to mute it. If the remote was used to set the mute you will need to get a remote to turn it off. I have a remote and muted a friends radio as a joke and he had to come over and have me turn the mute off. You could probably go to a stereo shop and have them turn the mute off.<BR>There is no way to turn the mute off/on without a remote or ungrounding the cell phone line if it is muted that way.||||reg||1
Z||000002||varnster||01-06-2001||04:44 PM||||I got it at best buy it was an open box buy<BR>but it came with no remote I didnt think this<BR>particular unit had a remote does any one know if this one has a remote option?||||reg||1
Z||000003||pred1tor83||01-06-2001||08:30 PM|||| <A HREF="http://www.carAudioForum.Com" TARGET=_blank>www.carAudioForum.Com</A>  <P><BR>ask your question there!!||||reg||6
Z||000004||My7Fieros||01-06-2001||10:20 PM||||Push the "ATT" button (may only be on your remote if you have one).||||reg||1
